### 1.2 Weng, J.H. et al. (2024). Mental wellness self-care in Singapore with mindline.sg.

**Citation:** Weng, J.H., Lim, H.A., Ho, C.S., & Ng, B.Y. (2024). Mental wellness self-care in Singapore with mindline.sg. JMIR Mental Health. DOI: 10.2196/44443

**Summary:** This paper evaluates mindline.sg, Singapore's national digital mental health platform launched by MOH. The platform received 447,000+ visitors in its first two years, demonstrating strong population-level engagement with digital mental health tools. The paper identifies persistent challenges including stigma, limited mental health literacy, and insufficient trained personnel — challenges that automated NLP screening could partially address. The authors note that adolescents and young adults are the most active demographic on the platform.

**Relevance to Pipeline:** Establishes that Singapore's digital mental health infrastructure is active and well-used. The pipeline proposed in this project is designed to integrate with mindline.sg as a medium-risk output channel, routing users identified by NLP screening to appropriate platform resources.

**Key Number:** 447,000+ visitors in first 2 years; adolescents most active demographic.

