### 1.3 Systematic Review (2026). Types and effectiveness of digital interventions for mental health literacy and help-seeking in adolescents (2021–2025).

**Citation:** Al-Rafidain Journal of Medical Sciences. (2026). Types and effectiveness of digital interventions for mental health literacy and help-seeking in adolescents.

**Summary:** This systematic review covers digital mental health interventions for adolescents across 2021–2025, evaluating their effectiveness in improving mental health literacy and help-seeking behaviour. Key findings include that digital interventions show consistent effectiveness in reducing stigma and improving help-seeking intentions, but adoption remains limited by awareness barriers and trust deficits. The review notes that interventions specifically designed for cultural context significantly outperform generic tools in Asian populations.

**Relevance to Pipeline:** Provides evidence base for why culturally-adapted digital tools outperform generic Western tools — directly supporting the rationale for building an Asian adolescent-specific NLP pipeline rather than deploying existing English-language tools.

**Key Finding:** Culturally-adapted digital interventions significantly outperform generic tools in Asian adolescent populations.

