### 2.3 Chim, J. et al. (2024). Overview of the CLPsych 2024 Shared Task.

**Citation:** Chim, J., Kochkina, E., Liakata, M., & Tsakalidis, A. (2024). Overview of the CLPsych 2024 Shared Task: Leveraging Large Language Models for Identifying Evidence of Suicidality Risk. ACL Anthology.

**Summary:** The CLPsych 2024 Shared Task focuses on improving the interpretability of LLMs in mental health analysis — specifically, identifying linguistic evidence of suicidality risk in Reddit posts. This task represents the gold standard benchmark for English-language mental health NLP evaluation. Participating systems demonstrated that LLMs can identify suicidality evidence with high accuracy when given structured prompting and domain-specific fine-tuning. The task also identified that most top-performing systems rely on English data and fail to generalise across languages and cultures.

**Relevance to Pipeline:** CLPsych 2024 provides the English-language benchmark against which the English component of this pipeline can be evaluated. The finding that top systems fail to generalise across languages directly motivates the multilingual approach of this project.

**Key Finding:** Top-performing English LLMs fail to generalise across languages — the primary gap this pipeline addresses.

